    "name": "Kadiravelayuda Suwami Kovil",
    "description": "Kadiravelayuda Suwami Kovil is a serene and historically rich temple located in Kalutara, Western Province, Sri Lanka. The temple stands as a testament to the rich cultural heritage of the region, dedicated to the deity Kadiravelayuda, a form of the Hindu god Vishnu. Its origins date back to the 13th century, and it has undergone several renovations over the centuries. The temple’s architecture reflects a blend of traditional Sinhalese and Tamil styles, featuring intricate carvings and colorful murals that narrate mythological stories. Visitors can explore the main shrine, which houses the deity’s statue, and the surrounding gardens that offer a tranquil environment. The temple also hosts various religious ceremonies and festivals, particularly during the Hindu New Year, which attract pilgrims from across the country. The temple’s peaceful ambiance and historical significance make it a must-visit for those interested in Sri Lanka’s cultural heritage.",
